This tests the intel_iommu driver with various possible configurations
from kernel parameters.

required parameters:

DMA_MODNAME:
	"intel_iommu"
	"amd_iommu"
	"arm_smmu"


For Intel:

DMA_IOMMU_CONF:
	"sm-on-lazy"   (requires an SPR or newer system, basically same hostreq as idxd or iaa. Likely can't enable in kpet-db/cki due to lack of systems for cki)
	"sm-on-strict" (requires an SPR or newer system, basically same hostreq as idxd or iaa. Likely can't enable in kpet-db/cki due to lack of systems for cki)
	"sm-on-pt"     (requires an SPR or newer system, basically same hostreq as idxd or iaa. Likely can't enable in kpet-db/cki due to lack of systems for cki)
	"lazy"
	"strict"
	"pt"
	"forcedac"
	"sp_off"
	"igfx_off"

For AMD:

DMA_IOMMU_CONF:
	"lazy"
	"strict"
	"pt"
	"off"
	"forcedac"
	"pgtbl_v2-lazy"
	"pgtbl_v2-strict"
	"pgtbl_v2-pt"     # this should fall back to v1 page tables, tests tries to verify that is the case

